issue.notes:
Investigation completed - this is a false positive alarm.

Root cause: Bug in NEEDLE/src/strand/pluck.rs:450-455. The starvation_alert_body() function chooses the wrong message when stats.open_count == 0.

Code at line 451-455:
  let message = if stats.open_count > 0 {
      "Pluck found no candidates but open beads exist"
  } else {
      "Pluck found no candidates and queue is empty"
  };

Expected behavior: When open_count == 0, message should be "queue is empty".
Actual behavior: Alert shows "open beads exist" but Open beads: 0.

Workspace state at time of investigation:
  - 100 closed beads (all trail-boss work complete)
  - 0 open beads
  - 1 in_progress bead (this alert itself)
  - Ready query: correctly returns empty array

The workspace is genuinely idle - all trail-boss Phase 8 beads are closed. No action needed, but NEEDLE should be fixed to prevent confusing false alarms.
